 4. ⚠️ Charted: America&#x27;s job jitters 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Pew Research Center. Chart: Axios 48% of U.S. adults are very concerned that people who want to work won't be able to find jobs, according to a Pew survey — the highest reading since it started asking the question five years ago, Axios' Courtenay Brown and Neal Rothschild write. 

 Half of Americans also say they're very concerned about AI's role in the economy, Pew found. Keep reading . 

 
 
