 7. 🩺 Pope Leo diagnosed with lung cancer 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Pope Leo XIV arrives at the Agostino Gemelli Polyclinic in Rome, where he underwent an operation to remove a lung nodule. Photo: Alessandra Tarantino/AP Pope Leo underwent surgery yesterday that confirmed he has lung cancer, Axios' Josephine Walker writes. 

 The news came just hours after doctors removed the lower lobe of his right lung. The Holy See Press Office said the cancer is lung adenocarcinoma, which earlier tests had led his medical team to suspect.

 Leo, 71, said Sunday that the nodule "was detected at a very early stage and is well localized." Keep reading . 

 
 
