 8. ⛳ 1 for the road: Trump&#x27;s tree timeout 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The trunks of large trees are wrapped in caution tape at East Potomac Golf Links in D.C. on Monday. Photo: Mark Schiefelbein/AP A federal judge yesterday ordered tree removal work to stop at East Potomac golf course through at least Oct. 26, Axios D.C.'s Cuneyt Dil writes. 

 The court granted a request to require three business days' notice before conducting additional work on the site, according to legal advocacy group Democracy Forward . Go deeper . 

 
 
